<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet>
  <title>2.12. Series solutions of ODEs intro</title>
  <alert>MTH 401</alert>

  <p>
    Sovling the wave equation on a disk results in Bessel's equation of order 
    <m>n</m>, a differential equation that requires a solution using <term>power series</term>.
    A <term>power series</term> centered at <m>x=a</m> has the form
    <md>
      <mrow>
      y(x) \amp = a_0 + a_1(x-a)+a_2(x-a)^2+a_3(x-a)^3+\cdots 
      </mrow>
      <mrow>
      \amp = \sum\limits_{n=0}^{\infty} a_n(x-a)^n.
      </mrow>
    </md>
     Most often we use a power series centered around <m>x=0</m>: <m>y(x) = \sum\limits_{n=0}^{\infty} a_nx^n</m>.
  </p>
  <p>
    We essentially "guess" the solution is in the form of a power series, then plug in our guess into the 
    differential equation and solve for the constants that make it true.
  </p>

  <exercise workspace="5in">
    <statement>
      <p>Find a power series solution for the initial value problem
  <md>
  \begin{aligned}
    y' + xy \amp  = 0 \\
    y(0) \amp  = 1
  \end{aligned}
  </md></p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise workspace="5in">
    <statement>
      <p>Find power series solutions of the following differential
  equation by finding the recurrence relation between the coefficients
  and writing the first four terms of two linear independent
  solutions.
  <md>
  y'' - xy' - y = 0.
  </md></p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise workspace="5in">
    <statement>
      <p>Use power series to find the general solution to the differential equation
  <md>
  y'' - 2xy' + 4y = 0.
  </md></p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

</worksheet>
